  "report_period": "Week 44 (25th Oct to 31st Oct 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Hero\" 178/2010 SWS, China (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed at region USD 26 mill. Note that back in September, the two- years-older sister vessel \"Alpha Prudence\" 178/2008 SWS, China (SS 01/2028, DD 04/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 24,75 mill. Nisshin Shipping committed their Ultramax \"Greenwich Pioneer\" 63/2020 Nantong, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at excess USD 32 mill basis T/C attached till Mar'25 at 16.500 usd/pd. For reference, the one-year-older \"Seacon Athens\" 63/2019 Nantong, China (SS 07/2029, DD 07/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold back in August at the same levels. On the Supramax sector, Korea Line Corp committed their \"Global Genesis\", \"Global Brave\", \"Global Frontier\" & \"Global Hope\" 57/2010 Stx Dalian, China (SS/DD 09/2025, SS/DD 05/2025, SS/DD 08/2025, SS/DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) were committed to undisclosed interests at high USD 12 mill each. For comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"H Juno\" 57/2011 Stx Dalian, China (SS/DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in July at USD 14 mill. The Handysize \"Indian Ocean\" 36/2011 Samjin, China (SS/DD 10/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed to Indonesian interests at USD 12,5 mill, while the sister vessel \"Caroline Selmer\" 35/2011 Samjin, China (SS/DD 07/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 12,6 mill. Remind you that the sister vessel \"Thomas Selmer\" 35/2011 Samjin, China (SS/DD 04/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold back in September at region USD 13 mill.",
    "tankers": "Zodiac Maritime have committed their LR1 \"Fulham Road\" 75/2013 Stx, Korea (SS 11/2028, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) to Greek interests at USD 44,6 mill. In addition, the older \"Octa Lune\" 73/2005 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) of Coral Shipping was committed to Chinese interests at region USD 20 mill. For reference, the one-year-older Japanese built \"Fair World\" 74/2008 Onomichi, Japan (SS 04/2029, DD 07/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold back in August at USD 20,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid usd 8,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Trips from China into Japan were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 8,000/10,000 pd. South American trips into Arabian Gulf-South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K/500K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Trips from China into Indonesia were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesia trips into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/14,000 pd. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 160K/180K. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd. On the period front, a Supramax was reported fixed in the usd 13,500 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery South East Asia.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Continental trips into US Gulf were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. South American trips into Continent or West Africa were reported at the level of usd 16,000/19,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
